Real-World Tier (TerraDS Upstream Modules)
=========================================

Real-world scenarios incorporate open-source Terraform modules sourced from
TerraDS (Zenodo record 20339474, concept DOI 10.5281/zenodo.14217385). Each scenario
preserves the module's original upstream licence text in its `PROVENANCE/LICENSE.upstream`
file and upstream metadata in `PROVENANCE/SOURCE.json`.

In accordance with Apache-2.0 Section 4(b) and upstream notices:
1. Host modules: Modified by removing top-level `provider` and `terraform` blocks to
   enable deterministic local evaluation against pinned provider versions. The canonical
   benchmark core (`terrapreserve_graft.tf`, `terrapreserve_graft_variables.tf`) is added
   alongside the host module.
2. Derived native modules: Modified by redacting literal database passwords on `aws_db_instance`
   resources and replacing them with `var.db_password`, accompanied by sensitive variable
   declarations in `terrapreserve_derived.tf`.
3. All custom benchmark synthesis code, graft definitions, and scenario records are licensed
   under CC-BY-4.0.


